---
description: Keep card edge effects aligned with perspective tilt
globs: src/ui/effects/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Perspective-Aware Effects

Card artwork is rendered with a `PerspectiveMesh`, while effect `Graphics` layers are flat siblings.

When drawing graphics or sprites that should hug the tilted card face, project local card coordinates through `projectPointToSurface` from `src/ui/effects/shared/surfaceProjection.ts` with the current `EffectFrameContext`.

Use this for border strokes, edge flames/lightning, hover impact points, and card-surface particles. Do not duplicate the projection math in effect definitions.

If an effect uses `getEffectTexture(...)`, ensure the host rendering path suspends with `use(effectsTexturesReady)` before creating effect runtimes. Missing this can create reload-dependent texture races and inconsistent effect brightness/fills.

For die edge effects, reuse `DIE_EDGE_POINTS` / `createDieEdgeLoop` from `src/ui/effects/shared/dieOutline.ts`. Do not duplicate die outline points or approximate dice with circles/hexes in individual effect definitions.

When applying `BlurFilter` to effect `Graphics`, always set a fixed local `filterArea`. Prefer `applyBlurredGlowForMount(...)` when creating the blur, or call `setGlowFilterAreaForMount(...)` after assigning custom blur filters. Animated blurred graphics without a bounded filter area can leave faint additive glow bleed in later filtered layers.
